# Machine-specific overrides for `npm run start`. Copy this file to .env and
# fill in real values there — .env is gitignored, this file is the tracked
# template and must only ever hold placeholders/comments.
#
# Most teammates won't need this file at all: once you've followed the
# README's "One-time setup" and created backend/agroguard/.venv and
# backend/agriquill/.venv, start-all.mjs finds them on its own.
#
# Use this only if you're intentionally pointing a backend at an interpreter
# that lives outside this workspace (e.g. a shared venv reused during local
# development before backend/agriquill had its own .venv). The path must
# exist — startup fails with a clear message otherwise, it never silently
# falls back to a global "python" on PATH.
AGROGUARD_PYTHON=
AGRIQUILL_PYTHON=
